d)","dish/paska-bread"],["Pâté","dish/pate"],["Pelmeni","dish/pelmeni"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Pirozhki","dish/pirozhki"],["Polonaise sauce","dish/polonaise-sauce"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Pozharsky cutlet","dish/pozharsky-cutlet"],["Rassolnik","dish/rassolnik"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Shchi","dish/shchi"],["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"],["Soured milk","dish/soured-milk"],["Syrniki","dish/syrniki"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/6f/2023_Sa%C5%82atka_jarzynowa_%281%29.jpg/500px-2023_Sa%C5%82atka_jarzynowa_%281%29.jpg","w":500,"h":367,"by":"Jacek Halicki","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2023_Sa%C5%82atka_jarzynowa_(1).jpg"}},"ingredient/raclette-du-valais":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/raclette-du-valais","n":"Raclette du Valais","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Raclette du Valais or Walliser Raclette (German) is a semi-hard Swiss cheese that is usually fashioned into a wheel of about 6 kg (13 lb). The Alpine cow milk-based dairy product is most commonly used for melting for the dish called raclette, but is also consumed as is."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-raclette-du-valais"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raclette_du_Valais"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine",[["Raclette","dish/raclette"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/57/Walliser_teller.jpg/500px-Walliser_teller.jpg","w":500,"h":430,"by":"Adrian Michael","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Walliser_teller.jpg"}},"ingredient/laminated-dough":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/laminated-dough","n":"Laminated dough","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Laminated dough is a culinary preparation consisting of many thin layers of dough separated by butter or other solid fat, produced by repeated folding and rolling. Such doughs may contain more than eighty layers. During baking, water in the butter vaporizes and expands, causing the dough to puff up and separate, while the lipids in the butter essentially fry the dough, resulting in a light, flaky product."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-laminated-dough"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laminated_dough"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Israeli cuisine","cuisine/israeli-cuisine",[["Ziva (dish)","dish/ziva-dish"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Nigella seeds","ingredient/nigella-seeds"],["Olive","ingredient/olive"],["Puff pastry","ingredient/puff-pastry"],["Sesame seeds","ingredient/sesame-seeds"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/90/Pate_feuilletee_2.jpg/500px-Pate_feuilletee_2.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Popo le Chien","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pate_feuilletee_2.jpg"}},"site/amiraspantry-com":{"t":"site","r":"site/amiraspantry-com","n":"Amira's Pantry","c":"#55b8ad","crumb":[["Recipe sites","sites"]],"sub":"Recipe site, amiraspantry.com","square":true,"suggested":true,"intro":[["Egyptian section of Amira's recipe blog, with koshari, hawawshi, feteer and sweets."]],"actions":[{"kind":"out","url":"https://amiraspantry.com","label":"Visit amiraspantry.com"}],"sections":[{"h":"Cuisines it covers","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Egyptian cuisine","ref":"cuisine/egyptian-cuisine","color":"#e46a3f","shape":"cuisine","sub":"Amira's Pantry","url":"https://amiraspantry.com/tag/egyptian-cuisine/"}]}]},